{
  "dom_id": "step-q84263",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=4\\sqrt[3]{t}-1.$ What is the total displacement of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=8?$",
  "worked_solution": "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{8}(4\\sqrt[3]{t}-1)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(3{t}^{4/3}-t){|}_{1}^{8} \\\\  & =[3(8)^{4/3}-8]-[3(1)^{4/3}-1] \\\\  & =[48-8]-[3-1] \\\\  & =40-2 \\\\  & =38.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=8$ is $38.$",
